course: dictionary
lesson: 6663
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Nutty can mean containing nuts, silly, or very keen on something. «They taste nutty and crunchy, and for her they are just a normal snack.» The clues are taste and snack, so nutty means containing nuts or tasting like nuts.
explain: Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one fits. «A nutty idea» does not mean an idea that tastes of nuts. The word idea tells you the meaning is silly or strange in a funny way. Always ask: what is the word describing?
explain: Nutty is informal, so you hear it in chatting and jokes more than in school reports. «As nutty as a fruitcake» means as silly and wacky as a fruitcake, which is a funny comparison about a person, not about a cake.
fact: Nutty has three main meanings: containing nuts or tasting like nuts, silly or crazy in a funny way, and very keen on something.
fact: «A nutty chocolate bar» means a chocolate bar with nuts in it.
fact: «A nutty professor» is a funny, wacky character who seems a bit crazy, often found in stories.
fact: «Nutty about football» means very keen on football. This meaning is informal.
fact: Foods with nuts can be dangerous for people with nut allergies, so always check labels for «may contain nuts».
exercise: «They taste nutty and crunchy, and for her they are just a normal snack.» What does nutty mean here? | *Containing nuts or tasting like nuts | Very old | Silly and crazy | Very keen on something
exercise: «He had a nutty idea to paint the school bus green.» What does nutty mean here? | Very keen on something | Very fast | *Silly or strange in a funny way | Containing nuts
exercise: Sam says «nutty about football». What does it mean? | Playing football badly | Covered in nuts | *Very keen on football | Asleep before the match
test: Which phrase uses nutty to mean containing nuts? | *«a nutty chocolate bar» | «a nutty idea» | «as nutty as a fruitcake» | «a nutty professor»
test: Why should you check labels for «may contain nuts»? | Because it tells you the price of the food | Because nutty means silly, so the label is a joke | *Because nutty foods can be dangerous for people with nut allergies | Because it shows the shop's name
exam: Jayden reads «a nutty idea» and «nutty about football». What is the difference in meaning? | The first means containing nuts, and the second means very old | *The first means silly or strange in a funny way, and the second means very keen on something | They mean exactly the same thing | Both mean containing nuts
